    "revision": "r1.1",
    "notes": [
      "r1: every presence and claim event between P1 and P3 (the agent's focus, selection and cells after each verb; claim start and end with the actor) is in turn-frames.json's timeline. P3's agent cells follow ruling 2",
      "the view is Ada's client (person:ada). isSelf and sameUser are worked out by the client; they are not sent",
      "all elements are addresses, as on the wire. Row addresses name KEYS, not row numbers: @sheet:1/row:r16 is the Totals row, row 18 at rev 20 and row 19 after rev 23",
      "focus, selection, pointer and viewport EXIST (kit 44c3c9ff). 'cells' is NEW (kit item VC): a cell caret plus range selections, each range one unit given by two corners",
      "a corner is {row, row_off, col, col_off}: the last keyed row (column) at or before the cell, and how many rows (columns) past it. null row means 'before the first keyed row', and row_off is then the row number. Offsets are 0 on a keyed row or column",
      "viewport, for a grid, is in cells (this addendum's rule, declared in the schema's grid slot): x = first visible column number, y = first visible row number, w = columns, h = rows, on the focus sheet. The kit stores it as it does today; it does not move it",
      "_a1 fields are annotations for checking, not on the wire: the view works them out from the corners and the numbering",
      "colours are placeholders for the hex colour K2 stamps at join",
      "mode is derived by the client: editing = holds a claim covering its cells or selection; selecting = has a selection or a range; else viewing",
      "presence needs K2 to relay element presence (contract r1.6 gap 10) and, for 'cells', the new frame and roster kind"
    ]
  },
